+# Tasks: Local User Account Manager (CLI)
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-user-accounts-cli/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: [plan.md](./plan.md), [spec.md](./spec.md), [research.md](./research.md), [data-model.md](./data-model.md), [contracts/cli-contract.md](./contracts/cli-contract.md), [contracts/store-format.md](./contracts/store-format.md), [quickstart.md](./quickstart.md)
+
+**Tests**: REQUIRED and included. Constitution Principle III makes every FR, SR
+and SC map to a named automated `pytest` test, and an unmapped requirement
+blocks completion. Test file names and test ids below are taken verbatim from
+plan.md's [requirement-to-test mapping](./plan.md#requirement-to-test-mapping)
+and [security mapping](./plan.md#security-requirement-mapping) — do not rename
+them.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story so each story can be
+implemented, tested and delivered independently.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3, US4)
+- Exact file paths are given in every task
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Single project, flat package (plan.md "Structure Decision"):
+
+- Source: `src/accounts/` — `__init__.py`, `__main__.py`, `cli.py`, `store.py`, `crypto.py`, `validation.py`, `errors.py`
+- Tests: `tests/`
+- Config: `pytest.ini`, `requirements-dev.txt` at repository root
+- Run form: `PYTHONPATH=src python -m accounts --store PATH COMMAND USERNAME` — no install step
+
+**Standing constraints for every task** (Constitution I, II, IV, V): standard
+library only in `src/`; no `except Exception`/bare `except`; no password, salt,
+digest, KDF parameter, store content or traceback in any output stream; no real
+credential material anywhere in the repository including fixtures.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)
+
+**Purpose**: Project skeleton, test harness, development dependency declaration
+
+- [ ] T001 Create the package and test skeleton: directories `src/accounts/` and `tests/`, and `src/accounts/__init__.py` containing only a module docstring and `__version__ = "1.0.0"` — no logic of any kind (plan.md Project Structure)
+- [ ] T002 Create `pytest.ini` at repository root with `pythonpath = src`, `testpaths = tests`, and a registered `markers` entry for `slow` (used by the 1 000-account, concurrency and crash-loop tests)
+- [ ] T003 [P] Create `requirements-dev.txt` at repository root containing only `pytest` — a development dependency never imported by `src/` (Constitution Principle I)
+- [ ] T004 [P] Create `tests/conftest.py` with the three shared fixtures named in plan.md: (a) a `tmp_path`-based store path fixture, (b) a subprocess runner that invokes the real executable as `[sys.executable, "-m", "accounts"]` with `PYTHONPATH=src`, piped stdin/stdout/stderr and `text=True`, returning `(status, stdout, stderr)`, and (c) a store-builder fixture that writes a syntactically valid store from **synthetic** base64 salt/hash values only — never a real derivation and never a plaintext password (Constitution "Secrets hygiene", SR-004)
+
+**Checkpoint**: `pytest` runs and collects zero tests without error.
