+- [ ] T013 Implement `locked_store(path)` as a context manager in `src/accounts/store.py`: `os.open(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(path)) or ".", os.O_RDONLY)` then `fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)`, held for the entire read–modify–write and released by closing the descriptor in a `finally` (SR-007, research R4). It MUST create no file of any kind — not the store, not a lock sidecar (FR-007). An `OSError` opening or locking the directory → `AccountsError(5, "error: cannot read store 'PATH': <errno description>")`
+- [ ] T014 Implement `load(path)` in `src/accounts/store.py` following store-format.md "Order of checks on load" exactly: (1) `open`; `ENOENT` → return the in-memory empty store `{"version": 1, "accounts": {}}` **without creating any file**, any other `OSError` → status 5 `cannot read store`; (2) `os.fstat(fd).st_size > 8388608` → status 5 `"error: store 'PATH' is too large: expected at most 8388608 bytes, received N"` **before reading a byte** (SR-006); (3) read and UTF-8 decode, `UnicodeDecodeError` → status 5 malformed; (4) `json.loads`, catching `json.JSONDecodeError` and `RecursionError` narrowly → status 5 malformed (`nesting too deep` for the latter; the one deliberate suppression recorded in plan.md Complexity Tracking)
+- [ ] T015 Implement `validate_document(doc)` in `src/accounts/store.py`: the document MUST be a JSON object with **exactly** the two keys `version` and `accounts` — any additional key, any missing key, any other type → `AccountsError(5, "error: store 'PATH' is malformed: <structural reason>")`. `version` MUST satisfy `type(v) is int and v == 1` (any other value → `unsupported version`); `accounts` MUST be a `dict` with at most `10000` members (more → `"error: store 'PATH' holds too many accounts: expected at most 10000, received N"`). Reasons name the shape problem, never a value (SR-009)
+- [ ] T016 Implement `validate_record(username, record)` in `src/accounts/store.py` as the SR-001 allow-list over **exactly these eight keys, no more and no fewer**, with the ranges quoted verbatim from store-format.md: `kdf` string exactly `"scrypt"`; `n` integer, power of two, `2 … 1048576`; `r` integer `1 … 32`; `p` integer `1 … 16`; `dklen` integer `16 … 64`; `salt` padded standard-alphabet base64 decoding to **exactly 16 bytes**; `hash` padded standard-alphabet base64 decoding to **exactly `dklen` bytes**; `failed_logins` integer `0 … 5`. Cross-field rule: `n * r * 128` MUST NOT exceed `201326592`. Every integer check is explicitly `type(v) is int` so `True`/`False` are rejected. The `accounts` key itself MUST satisfy the 3–32-character `[A-Za-z0-9_]` username rule. One invalid record fails the whole load under status 5 — never repaired, guessed at, skipped or partially loaded
+- [ ] T017 [P] Implement `serialise(doc)` in `src/accounts/store.py` as `json.dumps(doc, ensure_ascii=True, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"))` plus one trailing `"\n"`, encoded UTF-8 — byte-deterministic for a given account set, which is what makes the SC-008 comparison a byte comparison (store-format.md Encoding, SR-002)
+- [ ] T018 Implement `atomic_write(path, data)` in `src/accounts/store.py` as the exact six-step write discipline of store-format.md: (1) `dir = dirname(realpath(path))`; (2) `fd = os.open(f"{dir}/.{name}.{secrets.token_hex(8)}.tmp", os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)` — unpredictable name, no overwrite, `0o600` set **at creation** (SR-003, SR-008); (3) write, `os.fsync(fd)`, `os.close(fd)`; (4) `os.replace(tmp, path)`; (5) `fsync` the directory descriptor; (6) on any `OSError` in steps 2–4, `os.unlink` the temporary file and raise `AccountsError(5, "error: cannot write store 'PATH': <errno description>")` so no temporary file survives a failure
+- [ ] T019 Implement `parse_args(argv)` in `src/accounts/cli.py` with `argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False, allow_abbrev=False)`: `--store` as a **required** option, `command` positional with `choices=("register", "login", "unlock", "passwd", "delete")` (this is SR-001's allow-list for the command name), `username` positional, nothing else accepted. Override `ArgumentParser.error` to raise `AccountsError(2, ...)` instead of exiting, emitting `"usage: python -m accounts --store PATH {register|login|unlock|passwd|delete} USERNAME"` for a shape problem and `"error: unknown command 'COMMAND': expected one of register, login, unlock, passwd, delete"` for a bad command (research R10, contracts/cli-contract.md)
