+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: no dependencies — start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: depends on Phase 1; **blocks every user story**
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: depends on Phase 2 only
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: depends on Phase 2; its implementation edits `cmd_login`, so it is sequenced **after** US1 in a single-developer run
+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: depends on Phase 2 only
+- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: depends on Phase 2 only
+- **Polish (Phase 7)**: depends on all four stories being complete (T048, T050, T053 exercise all five commands)
+
+### Within Phase 2
+
+- T005 (`errors.py`) first — every other module raises `AccountsError`
+- T006 → T007, T008 (constants before the rules that use them)
+- T009 → T010, T011 → T012 (parameters, then salt/derive, then verify)
+- T013, T014, T015, T016, T017 → T018 (`load` needs `validate_document` and `validate_record`; `atomic_write` needs `serialise`)
+- T021 (sanitiser) before T007's message formatting is finalised
+- T019, T020, T021 → T022 → T023 (`main` dispatches, `__main__` calls `main`)
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: independent after Phase 2. Delivers the MVP
+- **US2 (P2)**: independent *in test* after Phase 2, but T036–T038 modify `cmd_login` written by T030, so it follows US1 in practice
+- **US3 (P3)**: independent after Phase 2; its tests register an account first, which US1 already provides
+- **US4 (P3)**: independent after Phase 2; touches no code any other story owns
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written first and MUST fail before implementation begins
+- Validation → store/crypto → command handler → dispatch registration
+- The story's own `pytest` files green before moving to the next priority
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- T003 and T004 in Setup
+- T006, T009, T017 in Foundational (different modules, no shared state)
+- All four US1 test files (T024–T027) — distinct files
+- T033, T034, T035 in US2; T041, T042 in US3
+- T048, T049, T050, T051, T052, T053 in Polish — six distinct test files
+- With multiple developers: after Phase 2, US3 and US4 can run alongside US1/US2 since `cmd_passwd` and `cmd_delete` touch no code the other stories modify
+
