+## Notes
+
+- `[P]` means a different file and no dependency on an incomplete task
+- `[Story]` maps a task to a user story for traceability; Setup, Foundational
+  and Polish tasks carry no story label
+- Test ids are fixed by plan.md's mapping tables — renaming one breaks the
+  Principle III audit in T054
+- Error messages are fixed by
+  [contracts/cli-contract.md](./contracts/cli-contract.md); `invalid
+  credentials` and `account locked` are byte-exact and carry no detail
+- Every write goes through `atomic_write` while the directory `flock` is held;
+  no command may read, decide and write outside that lock (SR-007)
+- Commit after each task or logical group; stop at any checkpoint to validate a
+  story independently
+- Avoid: creating a store file from any command other than `register`,
+  validating a `passwd` new password before authenticating, storing a `locked`
+  flag, and echoing anything from the store into a message